  "notes": "A formal word frequently used in news reporting, international relations, and legal contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {報復|ほうふく}{攻撃|こうげき} (retaliatory attack)\n- {報復|ほうふく}{措置|そち} (retaliatory measures)\n- {報復|ほうふく}を{恐|おそ}れる (to fear retaliation)\n- {報復|ほうふく}の{連鎖|れんさ} (chain of retaliation)\n- {報復|ほうふく}{関税|かんぜい} (retaliatory tariffs)\n\nUSAGE:\nMore formal than {仕返|しかえ}し, which is used in everyday and personal contexts. {報復|ほうふく} carries a heavier, more serious tone and is appropriate for geopolitical, military, and legal discourse.",
